:Class Remote
⍝ raylib in a browser: the raylibAPL functions that ui/App.apln uses, for one browser connected over a WebSocket.
⍝ The browser runs web/client, raylib compiled to WebAssembly, which only draws what it is sent and reports input.
⍝ Messages are lines of text. To the browser:
⍝   W width height title          InitWindow
⍝   F, then one line per call     a frame: C clear, R rectangle, O circle, o circle outline, L line, T text
⍝   Q                             CloseWindow
⍝ From the browser:
⍝   H w32 … w255                  hello: widths of the default font's glyphs for ⎕UCS 32…255, so MeasureText is computed here
⍝   I mx my sw sh rw rh|b…|k…     input since the last report: mouse, screen and render sizes, buttons and keys pressed
⍝ The browser answers each frame with one input report, so EndDrawing waits for the input that the next frame reads.
    ⎕IO←0

    :Field Public KeyboardKey      ⍝ raylibAPL's enums, so key and button codes are raylib's
    :Field Public MouseButton
    :Field Public Connected←1
    :Field Public Wait←30          ⍝ seconds to wait for the browser before treating it as gone

    :Field lib                     ⍝ Conga root and connection the browser is on
    :Field con
    :Field tok←0                   ⍝ token the session thread waits on for messages
    :Field inbox←⍬                 ⍝ messages received but not yet read
    :Field part←''                 ⍝ a message whose final fragment has not arrived
    :Field glyphs←⍬
    :Field frame←⍬                 ⍝ lines of the frame being drawn
    :Field input                   ⍝ the latest input report

    ∇ Make(l c rl)
      :Access Public
      :Implements Constructor
      (lib con)←l c
      KeyboardKey←rl.KeyboardKey ⋄ MouseButton←rl.MouseButton
      input←⎕NS ⍬ ⋄ input.(mouse size render buttons keys)←(0 0)(0 0)(0 0)⍬ ⍬
    ∇

⍝ Connection, called by web/Server.aplc from its own thread

    ∇ Receive(data fin)
      :Access Public
      part,←data ⋄ →fin↓0
      inbox,←⊂part ⋄ part←''
      ⎕TPUT tok
    ∇

    ∇ Disconnect
      :Access Public
      Connected←0
      ⎕TPUT tok
    ∇

    ∇ r←Next;t
    ⍝ the next message from the browser, or '' once it has gone
      :While Connected∧0=≢inbox
          :If 0=≢Wait ⎕TGET tok ⋄ Connected←0 ⋄ :EndIf
      :EndWhile
      →(0=≢inbox)⍴0⊣r←''
      (r inbox)←(⊃inbox)(1↓inbox)                ⍝ one statement: the server thread appends to inbox
    ∇

    Send←{Connected:0⊣lib.Send con(⍵ 1) ⋄ 0}
    Fmt←{'-'@('¯'∘=)⍕⍵}                          ⍝ numbers as C reads them
    Line←{frame,←⊂⍺,' ',Fmt ⍵ ⋄ 0}
    Nums←{⊃(//)⎕VFI ⍵}

    ∇ Read msg;b;k;n
    ⍝ take an input report
      →('I'≠⊃msg)⍴0
      (n b k)←Nums¨1↓¨{(⍵='|')⊂⍵}'|',1↓msg
      input.(mouse size render)←↓3 2⍴n ⋄ input.(buttons keys)←b k
    ∇

⍝ Window

    ∇ InitWindow(w h title);msg
      :Access Public
      tok←⎕TID
      Send'W ',(Fmt w h),' ',title
      :Repeat ⋄ msg←Next ⋄ :Until (0=≢msg)∨'H'=⊃msg
      glyphs←Nums 1↓msg
      Read Next                                   ⍝ the browser follows its hello with a first input report
    ∇

    ∇ CloseWindow x
      :Access Public
      →Connected↓0 ⋄ {}lib.Send con('Q' 1)1               ⍝ close the connection once Q has gone
    ∇

    ∇ SetTargetFPS x
      :Access Public
    ∇

    ∇ r←WindowShouldClose x
      :Access Public
      r←(~Connected)∨KeyboardKey.KEY_ESCAPE∊input.keys
    ∇

    ∇ r←GetScreenWidth x
      :Access Public
      r←⊃input.size
    ∇

    ∇ r←GetScreenHeight x
      :Access Public
      r←1⊃input.size
    ∇

    ∇ r←GetRenderWidth x
      :Access Public
      r←⊃input.render
    ∇

    ∇ r←GetRenderHeight x
      :Access Public
      r←1⊃input.render
    ∇

⍝ Input

    ∇ r←GetMousePosition x
      :Access Public
      r←input.mouse
    ∇

    ∇ r←IsKeyPressed k
      :Access Public
      r←k∊input.keys
    ∇

    ∇ r←IsMouseButtonPressed b
      :Access Public
      r←b∊input.buttons
    ∇

⍝ Drawing

    ∇ BeginDrawing x
      :Access Public
      frame←,⊂'F'
    ∇

    ∇ EndDrawing x
      :Access Public
      Send¯1↓∊frame,¨⎕UCS 10
      Read Next
    ∇

    ∇ r←ClearBackground c
      :Access Public
      r←'C'Line c
    ∇

    ∇ r←DrawRectangle(x y w h c)
      :Access Public
      r←'R'Line x y w h,c
    ∇

    ∇ r←DrawCircle(x y rad c)
      :Access Public
      r←'O'Line x y rad,c
    ∇

    ∇ r←DrawCircleLines(x y rad c)
      :Access Public
      r←'o'Line x y rad,c
    ∇

    ∇ r←DrawLine(x0 y0 x1 y1 c)
      :Access Public
      r←'L'Line x0 y0 x1 y1,c
    ∇

    ∇ r←DrawText(t x y s c)
      :Access Public
      frame,←⊂'T ',(Fmt x y s,c),' ',' '@(∊∘(⎕UCS 10 13))⍕t ⋄ r←0
    ∇

    ∇ r←MeasureText(t s);n;sp
      :Access Public
    ⍝ raylib's MeasureText with the default font: glyph widths scaled from its base size 10, plus spacing size÷10 between glyphs
      t←,⍕t ⋄ n←(⎕UCS t)-32 ⋄ n[⍸~n∊⍳≢glyphs]←31   ⍝ glyphs the font lacks are drawn as '?'
      s←10⌈s ⋄ sp←⌊s÷10
      r←⌊((s÷10)×+/glyphs[n])+sp×0⌈¯1+≢t
    ∇

:EndClass
